    kind: work_item  # f0e5
    title: "validation_report.schema_version='0.1' vs bm.schema_version='0.13.0'; independent sub-schema versioning with undocumented mapping"  # f0e5
    status: todo_hard  # f0e5
    priority: 4  # f0e5
    parent: INV-luhur-sital-lonar-tagiv-kuzab-mokol-jikot-fosug  # f0e5
    tags:  # f0e5
    - dogfooding  # f0e5
    - schema_drift  # f0e5
    - fold_audit_2026_06_03  # f0e5
    isbefore: []  # f0e5
    duplicate_of: []  # f0e5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f0e5
    pr_ref:  # f0e5
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family F). Stand-alone finding F23.5 previously folded onto INV-luhur. Full evidence remains on INV-luhur's pass-23 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`validation_report.schema_version='0.1'` vs `bm.schema_version='0.13.0'` — independent sub-schema versioning, relationship undocumented.\n\nThe new `validation_report` section (added by INV-sugat Phase 0) carries its own schema_version field. The relationship between the two version timelines is undocumented at spec.md or in any external mapping. A consumer reading `bm.schema_version=0.13.0` cannot determine the `validation_report`'s sub-schema version. If `validation_report`'s structure changes (e.g., violation record format), consumers using `bm.schema_version` as the validity gate get silent breakage.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEach sub-schema in the wire format has a documented version-mapping relationship to the top-level `schema_version`. Three options:\n\n1. **Consolidate to single version**: drop `validation_report.schema_version`; the top-level `schema_version` becomes the gate for every sub-schema.\n2. **Top-level mapping field**: add `bm.sub_schemas = {\"validation_report\": \"0.1\", ...}` so consumers can detect changes per-sub-schema.\n3. **Document the relationship in spec.md**: `bm.schema_version` ranges map to specific `validation_report.schema_version` values via a documented table.\n\nOption (1) is simplest; option (2) is most future-proof.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nPath (1): remove `validation_report.schema_version` from the writer; document that top-level `bm.schema_version` covers all sub-schemas. Smallest change.\n\nPath (2): add `sub_schemas` mapping at the top level; populate from each sub-schema writer at serialization time. Lets sub-schemas evolve independently.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F23.5** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-02T04:37:45 (pass-23 batch; paragraph beginning \"(F23.5) validation_report.schema_version='0.1' vs bm.schema_version='0.13.0'\").\n\nLab notebook: pass 23 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-luhur**.\n- Family F siblings."  # f0e5
    fields: {}  # f0e5
